        "        bibliography: ../../../rehear.bib\n",
        "        self-contained: true\n",
        "author: Jacopo Tissino\n",
        "date: 2025-03-31\n",
        "subtitle: Moriond 2025\n",
        "title: Parameter estimation with the Lunar Gravitational Wave Antenna\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# What is LGWA?\n"
      ],
      "id": "bd5f97bf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts import *"
      ],
      "id": "4e27d908",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "![](../figures/LGWA_crater_lighter.png){height=75% fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\\footnotesize Figure from the LGWA collaboration.\n",
        "\n",
        "# LGWA payload\n",
        "\n",
        "![](../figures/LGWApayload.png){height=75% fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\\footnotesize Figure from [van Heijningen et al., 2023](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/133/24/244501/2899601/The-payload-of-the-Lunar-Gravitational-wave).\n",
        "\n",
        "# LGWA readout \n",
        "\n",
        "![](../figures/squid-readout.png){height=75% fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\\footnotesize Figure from [van Heijningen et al., 2023](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/133/24/244501/2899601/The-payload-of-the-Lunar-Gravitational-wave).\n",
        "\n",
        "# Gravitational wave response\n",
        "\n",
        "How does this readout noise translate to noise on our measurement of gravitational waves?\n",
        "\n",
        "We assume that the response function from the gravitational polarizations $h_{ij}(t)$ to the\n",
        "displacement at the sensor $s(t)$ is _linear_: in the frequency domain,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ s(f) = L(f) D_{ij} h_{ij}(f)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "- $L(f)$ is the __response function__: with the dimensions of a length, is the displacement amplitude corresponding \n",
        "to a monochromatic unit strain;\n",
        "- $D_{ij} = n_i b_j$ is a __pattern function__, where $b_j$ is a tangent unit vector to the surface while $n_i$ is normal to it.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Structure of LGWA\n",
        "\n",
        "LGWA is planned to have:\n",
        "\n",
        "- 4 __stations__, to reduce overall noise and perform active cancellation;\n",
        "- for each station, two orthogonal __horizontal measurement channels__.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Strain noise\n",
        "\n",
        "If we have:\n",
        "\n",
        "- an estimate for the PSD of the detector __displacement noise__, $S_\\text{disp}(f)$,\n",
        "- an estimate of the lunar __response__ $L(f)$,\n",
        "- the number of stations $N$,\n",
        "\n",
        "we can compute the strain noise as \n",
        "\n",
        "$$ S_{\\text{strain}} (f) = \\frac{S _{\\text{disp}}(f)}{N L^2(f)}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# LGWA estimated noise\n",
        "\n",
        "![](../figures/LGWA_sensitivity.png){height=75% fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "# The multiband concept\n",
        "\n",
        "![](../figures/Multiband_concept.pdf){height=75% fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "# The reference frame problem\n",
        "\n",
        "The frequency-domain waveform at the detector has a travel time factor from the center of the reference frame:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ h(f) \\propto \\exp( i \\vec{k} \\cdot (\\vec{r} - \\vec{r}_0))\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The center $\\vec{r}_0$ should be rigidly connected with the SSB, but it can be elsewhere!\n",
        "\n",
        "# Sky position measurement - 1 month of observation\n"
      ],
      "id": "d9b72283"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from thesis_scripts import *\n",
        "import yaml\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(data_path / 'gw170817_lgwa_median.yaml') as f:\n",
        "    params = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "def fig_args(radius, params):\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'ra_lims': (\n",
        "            np.rad2deg(params['ra']-radius), \n",
        "            np.rad2deg(params['ra']+radius)\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        'dec_lims': (\n",
        "            np.rad2deg(params['dec']-radius), \n",
        "            np.rad2deg(params['dec']+radius)\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        'mollweide': False\n",
        "    }"
      ],
      "id": "5c8e0294",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts.mismatch_plots_lgwa import mismatch_plot\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.simple_bns_waveforms import time_to_merger_simple_inverse, SUN_MASS_SECONDS\n",
        "\n",
        "fmin = time_to_merger_simple_inverse(-3600*24*60, params['chirp_mass']*SUN_MASS_SECONDS)\n",
        "n_grid = 125\n",
        "\n",
        "ax = mismatch_plot(\n",
        "    params, \n",
        "    np.geomspace(fmin, 3, num=500), \n",
        "    n_grid=n_grid, \n",
        "    cache_name='cache/bns_recentered_2months', \n",
        "    **fig_args(np.deg2rad(2), params)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "11874b5b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Sky position measurement - 1 year\n"
      ],
      "id": "90534d5a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fmin = time_to_merger_simple_inverse(-3600*24*365.25, params['chirp_mass']*SUN_MASS_SECONDS)\n",
        "    \n",
        "ax = mismatch_plot(\n",
        "    params, \n",
        "    np.geomspace(fmin, 3, num=500), \n",
        "    n_grid=n_grid, \n",
        "    cache_name='cache/bns_recentered_1year', \n",
        "    **fig_args(np.deg2rad(2), params)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "d11ad309",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Sky position measurement - early warning\n"
      ],
      "id": "3203cf93"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fmin = time_to_merger_simple_inverse(-3600*24*365.25, params['chirp_mass']*SUN_MASS_SECONDS)\n",
        "fmax = time_to_merger_simple_inverse(-3600*24*30, params['chirp_mass']*SUN_MASS_SECONDS)\n",
        "    \n",
        "ax = mismatch_plot(\n",
        "    params, \n",
        "    np.geomspace(fmin, fmax, num=500), \n",
        "    n_grid=n_grid, \n",
        "    cache_name='cache/bns_recentered_ew', \n",
        "    # cache_name=None, \n",
        "    **fig_args(np.deg2rad(2), params)\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "c90ffb32",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Mass constraints\n"
      ],
      "id": "5823eaa4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts.plotting import plot_contours\n",
        "from matplotlib import ticker\n",
        "from matplotlib.lines import Line2D\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.plotting import make_arcmin_grid\n",
        "from thesis_scripts import data_path\n",
        "import yaml\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from cmcrameri import cm\n",
        "\n",
        "cmap_full = cm.devon\n",
        "cmap_ew = cm.lajolla\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_legend():\n",
        "\n",
        "    custom_lines = [\n",
        "        # Line2D([0], [0], color=cmap_ew(.5), markersize=10, marker='o', lw=0),\n",
        "        Line2D([0], [0], color=cmap_full(.8), markersize=10, marker='o', lw=0),\n",
        "        Line2D([0], [0], color=cmap_full(.4), markersize=10, marker='o', lw=0),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    plt.legend(\n",
        "        custom_lines, \n",
        "        [\n",
        "            # f'Early warning (4.5 months to merger, SNR 20)',\n",
        "            # f'Full bandwidth (3 hours to merger, SNR 28)',\n",
        "            '50\\% probability contained',\n",
        "            '90\\% probability contained',\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "run_folder = data_path / 'bns_test'\n",
        "\n",
        "injection_params = yaml.safe_load((run_folder / 'injection_parameters.yaml').read_text())\n",
        "\n",
        "# post_ew = pd.read_csv(data_path / 'ew_gw170817_run' / 'chains' / 'equal_weighted_post.txt', sep=' ')\n",
        "post_full = pd.read_csv(run_folder / 'chains' / 'equal_weighted_post.txt', sep=' ')\n",
        "\n",
        "# ra_lims = (3.442, 3.449)\n",
        "# dec_lims = (-0.412, -0.405)\n",
        "\n",
        "# filter_indices = (\n",
        "#     (post_ew_pre['ra'] > ra_lims[0]).to_numpy() & \n",
        "#     (post_ew_pre['ra'] < ra_lims[1]).to_numpy() & \n",
        "#     (post_ew_pre['dec'] > dec_lims[0]).to_numpy() & \n",
        "#     (post_ew_pre['dec'] < dec_lims[1]).to_numpy()\n",
        "# )\n",
        "\n",
        "# print(f'Filtering out {len(filter_indices) - sum(filter_indices)} outliers')\n",
        "\n",
        "# post_ew = post_ew_pre.iloc[filter_indices]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# fig = plt.figure(figsize=(5.2, 5.5))\n",
        "\n",
        "mc = injection_params['chirp_mass']\n",
        "\n",
        "x = np.linspace(-6e-7, 6e-7, num=500)\n",
        "y = np.linspace(0.86, 0.94, num=500)\n",
        "\n",
        "# plot_contours(post_ew['chirp_mass']-mc, post_ew['mass_ratio'], ax=plt.gca(), levels=[.9], cmap=cmap_ew, x=x, y=y, N=500)\n",
        "plot_contours(\n",
        "    post_full['chirp_mass']-mc, \n",
        "    post_full['mass_ratio'], ax=plt.gca(), levels=[.5, .9], cmap=cmap_full, x=x, y=y, N=500)\n",
        "plt.grid(which='both')\n",
        "plt.xlim(-2e-7, 2e-7)\n",
        "plt.scatter(0, injection_params['mass_ratio'], marker='x', c='black')\n",
        "plt.gca().xaxis.set_major_locator(ticker.FixedLocator(np.arange(-2, 4, 1)*1e-7))\n",
        "plt.gca().xaxis.set_major_formatter(ticker.FixedFormatter(\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        '$- 2 \\\\times 10^{-7}$',\n",
        "        '$-10^{-7}$',\n",
        "        '$0$',\n",
        "        '$ 10^{-7}$',\n",
        "        '$2 \\\\times 10^{-7}$',\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel('$\\mathcal{M} - \\mathcal{M}_0 [ M_{\\odot}]$')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('$q = m_2 / m_1$')\n",
        "make_legend()\n",
        "_ = plt.title('Mass constraints')"
      ],
      "id": "0677608a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Sky localization\n"
      ],
      "id": "08ed895b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ra_lims = np.deg2rad([197+24/60, 197+36/60])\n",
        "dec_lims = np.deg2rad([-24+35/60, -24+40/60])\n",
        "# fig=plt.figure(figsize=(5.2, 5.5))\n",
        "\n",
        "# plot_contours(post_ew['ra'], post_ew['dec'], ax=plt.gca(), levels=[.9], cmap=cmap_ew)\n",
        "plot_contours(post_full['ra'], post_full['dec'], ax=plt.gca(), levels=[.5, .9], cmap=cmap_full, N=500)\n",
        "plt.scatter(injection_params['ra'], injection_params['dec'], marker='x', c='black')\n",
        "\n",
        "make_arcmin_grid(plt.gca(), ra_lims, dec_lims)\n",
        "plt.grid(which='minor', lw=.5)\n",
        "plt.grid(which='major', lw=1)\n",
        "plt.gca().set_aspect('equal')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Right ascension')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Declination')\n",
        "make_legend()\n",
        "_ = plt.title('Sky location constraints')"
      ],
      "id": "72208bf8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Phase constraints\n"
      ],
      "id": "bde4192e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_likelihood import LunarLikelihood\n",
        "from thesis_scripts.lgwa_pe.lgwa_nested_sampling import from_bilby\n",
        "like = LunarLikelihood()\n",
        "like.compute_center(injection_params['time_at_center'])\n",
        "\n",
        "f = np.geomspace(0.086816181214, 3, num=2000)\n",
        "\n",
        "hx_0, hy_0 = like.projected_waveform(f, from_bilby(injection_params))\n",
        "\n",
        "ratios_to_plot = 2_000\n",
        "ratios = np.empty((2, ratios_to_plot, len(f)), dtype=complex)\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(ratios_to_plot):\n",
        "    params = from_bilby(post_full.iloc[i].to_dict())\n",
        "    hx, hy = like.projected_waveform(f, params)\n",
        "    ratios[0, i, :] = hx/hx_0\n",
        "    ratios[1, i, :] = hy/hy_0"
      ],
      "id": "e1f9de4c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from thesis_scripts.plotting import add_time_to_merger_axis\n",
        "cmap = plt.get_cmap('Blues')\n",
        "\n",
        "phase_diffs = np.sort(np.angle(ratios), axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axs = plt.subplots(2, 1, sharex=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "for percentile in [.5, .9]:\n",
        "    for i in range(2):\n",
        "        i_1 = int(ratios_to_plot*percentile/2.)\n",
        "        i_2 = int(ratios_to_plot*(1-percentile/2.))\n",
        "        axs[i].fill_between(f, \n",
        "            phase_diffs[i, i_1],\n",
        "            phase_diffs[i, i_2],\n",
        "            color=cmap(percentile)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        axs[i].plot(f,\n",
        "            phase_diffs[i, i_1],\n",
        "            c='black', lw=.5\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        axs[i].plot(f, \n",
        "            phase_diffs[i, i_2],\n",
        "            c='black', lw=.5\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        axs[i].set_xscale('log')\n",
        "        axs[i].set_ylim(-0.2, 0.2)\n",
        "\n",
        "axs[0].set_xlim(f[0], f[-1])\n",
        "axs[0].set_title('$x$ channel')\n",
        "axs[1].set_title('$y$ channel')\n",
        "axs[0].set_ylabel('Phase constraint [rad]')\n",
        "axs[1].set_ylabel('Phase constraint [rad]')\n",
        "axs[1].set_xlabel('Frequency [Hz]')\n",
        "add_time_to_merger_axis(axs[0], params['chirp_mass'])"
      ],
      "id": "10a6604d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Open problems: noise and moonquakes\n",
        "\n",
        "- Can we demonstrate active noise cancellation?\n",
        "- LGWA data will have gaps when moonquakes get too strong: how much do they impact PE?\n",
        "\n",
        "# Open problems: response calibration\n",
        "\n",
        "- We are assuming a known lunar response.\n",
        "- How does uncertainty there translate into parameter estimation?\n",
        "- Can we demonstrate the \"multibanding calibration trick\"?\n",
        "\n",
        "# Open problems: parameter estimation\n",
        "\n",
        "- likelihood acceleration (relative binning or similar)\n",
        "- analytical marginalizations (e.g. in phase)\n",
        "- different sources\n",
        "    - IMBH\n",
        "    - stellar BBH\n",
        "    - DWD\n",
        "    - ..."
      ],
      "id": "c0269fc1"
    }
